_site/
.github/vale/styles/*
!.github/vale/styles/config/
!.github/vale/styles/config/ignore/
!.github/vale/styles/config/vocabularies/
.quarto/
# LaTeX intermediates kept by `quarto render --to pdf ... keep-tex: true`
# (cv.tex, posts/*.tex, etc.) and lualatex's own auxiliary outputs. Build
# artifacts, not sources.
*.aux
*.bkm
*.bbl
*.blg
*.toc
*.log
/.pytest_cache/
/.ruff_cache/
/.states/
/.quarto/
**/*.quarto_ipynb
_freeze/
site_libs/
# Eleventy build output
_eleventy_site/
# Staged passthrough for Eleventy. Regenerated by scripts/site/stage-public.mjs
# from the tracked sources at the repo root plus the Quarto build output, so it
# is a copy and never a second source of truth.
public/
# Everything under src/content is generated from the Quarto sources and the
# _includes/entities files by scripts/site/migrate_posts.py. Edit the .qmd and
# .yml files, not these.
src/content/
# Minified stylesheet, written by scripts/site/minify-css.mjs.
build/
# Talk map, drawn at build time by scripts/site/build_talkmap.py. The geocode
# cache it reads (_cache/geocache.json) is committed; the map is derived.
src/eleventy/_includes/talk-map.njk
# Areas of expertise circle packing, drawn at build time by
# scripts/site/build_expertise.py from the committed scores in
# _cache/expertise.json. The picture is derived.
src/eleventy/_includes/expertise.njk

# --- agent tooling ---
# AGENTS.md is deliberately NOT ignored: it is the only orientation document a
# new contributor or a coding agent gets, so it has to ship with the clone.
# Scratch state stays out:
.kb/
graphify-out/
*.agent-scratch*

# Source images (global gitignore has *.png/*.svg/*.ico but these are project source assets)
!images/
!src/eleventy/static/logos/
cv.tex
cv-academic.tex
